# GitHub public quality (kms-secp256k1-api)

Treat every README, CHANGELOG, and Release note as public.

## Product voice

- **kms-secp256k1-api** is an AWS KMS-backed HTTP API for secp256k1 key ops (Ethereum / Cosmos / Casper modes) plus Docker.
- Keep AWS-only honesty in public docs; do not invent non-AWS key backends as product claims.

## Keep out of committed product text

- Host-absolute paths
- Credential filenames, token recipes, SSH key paths, remote aliases
- Internal fork / Approve / agent merge process
- Cursor plan or stage IDs
- CI drama ("re-cut", overwrite recipes) in CHANGELOG / Release notes

## Conventional commits and PRs

```text
<type>(optional-scope): summary in imperative
```

Types: `feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `refactor` | `test` | `chore` | `ci`.

PR title matches. Body: Summary + Test plan. No "Made with Cursor".
